  "crash_cause": "ScoreTracker was created with NewObject in AArenaGameMode::BeginPlay but held in a raw UObject pointer without UPROPERTY, so it was not rooted and the garbage collector destroyed it (log: 'LogGarbage: Collecting garbage: 412 objects purged' ~15s before the fatal EXCEPTION_ACCESS_VIOLATION reading address 0xffffffffffffffff in UArenaScoreTracker::AddPoints called from AArenaGameMode::OnGoalScored). The first goal after that GC dereferenced the dangling object and crashed the shipping build.",
  "no_colors_cause": "The palette asset /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary is loaded dynamically by string path in BeginPlay, so the cooker found no hard reference to it and did not include it in the packaged build; Config/DefaultGame.ini only force-cooked /Game/Data/Effects. The packaged run therefore logged \"Couldn't find file for package /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary\" and \"Palette is null, using fallback gray\", leaving the arena colorless. The editor works because it loads loose .uasset files directly, bypassing cooking.",
  "fixes": [
    "Source/PixelArena/ArenaGameMode.h: ScoreTracker is now UPROPERTY() TObjectPtr so GC roots it.",
    "Source/PixelArena/ArenaGameMode.cpp: LoadObject uses the package path /Game/Data/Palettes/DA_Primary, and OnGoalScored guards against null Stats/ScoreTracker/Hud.",
    "Config/DefaultGame.ini: added +DirectoriesToAlwaysCook=(Path=\"/Game/Data/Palettes\") so the palette data assets are cooked into the packaged build."
  ]
}
